1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,746
This animal has 9 brains, 3 hearts, and

2
00:00:02,746 --> 00:00:03,520
blue blood.

3
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:06,116
The octopus has around 500 million

4
00:00:06,116 --> 00:00:08,220
neurons, about as many as a dog.

5
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:10,500
But two thirds of them aren't in its head.

6
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:11,660
They're in its arms.

7
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:13,780
Each arm has its own mini brain.

8
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:16,460
It can taste, touch and move on its own.

9
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:18,400
But the main brain can still step in and

10
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:18,900
take control.

11
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:21,207
3 hearts: two pump blood past the gills,

12
00:00:21,207 --> 00:00:22,880
one pumps it around the body.

13
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:25,472
But when it swims, that body heart goes

14
00:00:25,472 --> 00:00:25,800
quiet.

15
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,213
And the blood is blue, because it carries

16
00:00:28,213 --> 00:00:29,920
oxygen with copper, not iron.

17
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,363
But in cold water with little oxygen,

18
00:00:32,363 --> 00:00:33,980
copper actually works better.

19
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:37,700
9 brains, 3 hearts, blue blood...

20
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:39,740
and zero bones.

21
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:41,480
